+/* MGVF mgvf-0023: the motor power field, and the bit that says the packet
+ * means it.
+ *
+ * WHAT IS ESTABLISHED, from the disassembly already written down in
+ * mgvf-0007's header: libScePad sets bit 0x40 of the SECOND flag byte on every
+ * DualSense output report it sends, in its own send path at 0x1800072e2,
+ * together with report byte 37 -- common byte 36 -- written at 0x18000737b,
+ * and bit 0x04 of report byte 39, which is flag2's haptic bit. mgvf-0007 named
+ * those three "vibration fields" and let them through untouched because
+ * nothing on this disk said what they meant.
+ *
+ * AND FROM THE CAPTURE, hid-175158.log, a Bluetooth session of a title driving
+ * the pad through that library: of 10,886 native 0x31 writes, 10,862 carry
+ * flag1 0x40 and 10,860 carry common byte 36 = 0x00; of the 283 that carry a
+ * motor, 282 carry both and the last is a truncated dump. So the library
+ * claims this field on every packet and writes zero into it.
+ *
+ * AND WHAT THE FIELD DOES, measured on 2026-09-11 in three runs whose packets
+ * were identical apart from this field. Unclaimed and claimed-with-zero felt
+ * THE SAME. Claimed with 0x77 dropped the rumble to almost imperceptible.
+ *
+ * So the pad honours the field and it is a REDUCTION, as the community's map
+ * says -- and the pad was already at no reduction, which is the half that
+ * matters. Nothing was attenuating this driver. The hypothesis this option was
+ * written to test, that a lingering reduction had been capping the haptic
+ * path, is dead, and mgvf-0021's comparison stands on its own evidence.
+ *
+ * IT IS AN ATTENUATOR AND NEVER A WAY TO GET MORE. There is no second
+ * intensity field: the gain scales the two motor bytes and saturates at 255,
+ * and this one can only take away from what they ask for. Worth keeping and
+ * not explained: 0x77 took away far more than the "-50% per nibble" that map
+ * implies.
+ *
+ * THE DEFAULT IS 0 AND NOT ABSENCE, which changed nothing on the pad measured
+ * and is still the better packet. A field left unclaimed carries whatever the
+ * pad was last told by anything else on the machine, and a pad quietly
+ * reduced by some other application would make this driver weak for a reason
+ * nothing in a trace could show. Claiming it at zero costs one bit and makes
+ * the state ours. It is what libScePad sends on every packet.
+ *
+ * The option still carries the BYTE rather than a yes or no: 0 to 255 sets the
+ * bit and writes that byte, and anything from 256 up goes back to leaving the
+ * field alone, which is what every build before this one sent. */
+#define DUALSENSE_COMMON_MOTOR_POWER    36
+#define DUALSENSE_FLAG1_MOTOR_POWER     0x40
+#define DUALSENSE_MOTOR_POWER_UNCLAIMED 0x100
 
 /* MGVF mgvf-0016: the shortest output report that carries the whole of what
  * the rewrite reads. flag2 is the last of the four bytes and it is common byte
@@ -329,7 +376,8 @@
